change:
  id: CHG-013
  title: Scrub mutation content at the durable and user-visible boundaries
  status: proposed
  intent: Apply credential scrubbing to proposer-authored mutation summary and patch text wherever it becomes durable or user-visible, rather than only to the proposer-evidence block.
  audience_level: developer
  relates_to:
    - RISK-006
    - ARCH-001
    - CON-002
    - SYS-001

deltas:
  - op: ADDED
    capability: candidate-bookkeeping-scrubbing
    requirement: Proposer-authored mutation text is redacted before it is committed or displayed.
    scenarios:
      - id: S1
        when: a proposer returns a mutation whose summary contains the configured model API key
        then: the candidate TOON written into the target repository contains a redaction marker rather than the key
      - id: S2
        when: a proposer returns a mutation whose patch contains an Authorization bearer header
        then: the committed candidate bookkeeping contains a redaction marker rather than the header value
      - id: S3
        when: a mutation containing a credential is reported before validation runs
        then: the reporter output contains a redaction marker rather than the credential, including for a candidate that is later discarded
      - id: S4
        when: the same mutation is dispatched through the CLI, the MCP tool and the interactive session
        then: all three produce identically redacted durable bookkeeping, because scrubbing is applied at the shared boundary rather than per entrypoint

acceptance:
  - scenario: S1
    test_id: pending
    layer: integration
  - scenario: S2
    test_id: pending
    layer: integration
  - scenario: S3
    test_id: pending
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S4
    test_id: pending
    layer: acceptance

tasks:
  - id: T1
    slice: add failing coverage showing mutation summary and patch reach durable bookkeeping unredacted
    status: pending
  - id: T2
    slice: apply scrubbing at the durable candidate-write boundary
    status: pending
  - id: T3
    slice: apply scrubbing at the reporter boundary so pre-validation output is redacted
    status: pending
  - id: T4
    slice: prove CLI, MCP and interactive session inherit the same redaction without per-entrypoint copies
    status: pending
  - id: T5
    slice: update README, wiki and RISK-006 with the resulting boundary
    status: pending

non_goals:
  - widening the sanitizer pattern set beyond the recorded API-key and bearer forms
  - sandboxing the proposer process
  - changing what a proposer is permitted to read

risks:
  - RISK-006 remains open until the durable and reporter boundaries are both covered
  - over-eager redaction could corrupt a legitimate patch whose content resembles a credential, so patterns must stay narrow and tested
